   "answer": "imagine the stock market is a giant game of dodgeball, and the people selling options are the kids holding the balls. \n\nwhen big Wall Street desks sell a ton of options to gamblers buying 0DTE lottos, they have to protect themselves so they don't get blown up. if the stock starts dropping, the kids holding the options have to panic-sell shares to stay safe, which makes the market crash faster like a boulder rolling downhill. \n\nif the stock goes up, they have to frantically buy shares to cover themselves, which acts like a giant trampoline bouncing the market higher. gamma exposure is just measuring how bouncy or slippery the floor is under the market based on all those options bets."
